# Graph output — ours (`.filigrio-out/`) and the oracle's (`graphify-out/`).
#
# Both patterns are **unanchored on purpose**: they match at any depth. The
# previous form listed two specific paths, which is how a 416 MB `.filigrio-out/`
# accumulated inside the next.js benchmark corpus (see `docs/perf/benchmarks.md`
# §9.2) — left there by a run that used the default store location.
#
# This is not only repo hygiene. The walker honours `.gitignore` (ADR-0022), so
# an un-ignored output directory is a directory the engine will **ingest as
# corpus on the next run** — it indexes its own output, inflating node counts
# with its own artifacts. Ignoring it is what makes that self-ingestion
# impossible.
.filigrio-out/
graphify-out/
